financial advisor, and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research before putting real

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:35.880
money to work. The week's biggest developments pulled together, what actually moved, why it matters,

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:45.860
and what to watch next. The NASDAQ composite fell from 26,518 to 25,298 over the week.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:56.700
The S&amp;P 500 moved from 7,501 down to 7,354. The TSX composite held near flat,

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:07.360
ending around 34,980. Our simulated portfolio sits at plus 1.04% year-to-date against the NASDAQs plus

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:16.600
14.13% year-to-date. That leaves us with negative 13.09% alpha for the year. Sector rotation

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:23.500
into healthcare and financials stood out while tech and energy lagged. This is the exact scenario where

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:29.320
our earlier rule about volume confirmation would have helped separate real moves from noise.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:37.300
M&amp;A driven sector rotation lets investors capture premium valuations when large pharma or tech firms

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:45.060
acquire next-generation platforms. The ABV 10.9 billion dollar emoji deal shows how acquires

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:51.980
pay-up for late-stage immunology assets that extend patent protected revenue, screened for targets

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:58.320
with Phase 2 or later data and low float. Set alerts on volume above the 20-day average once

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:06.000
the announcement hits. The pattern has worked best in 2021-2023 biotech rallies when acquireer

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:13.680
cash balances exceeded $5 billion. Risk is regulatory delay or integration failure that erodes the

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:20.640
initial pop. Use your broker's M&amp;A calendar filter plus a simple relative strength scan versus the

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:27.280
XBI ETF to time entries. Dividend growth investing focuses on companies that consistently raise

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:33.920
pay-outs over time rather than chasing the highest current yield. Screening TSX listed dividend

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:40.320
aristocrats on platforms like WealthSimple or QuestTrade using five-year dividend growth rates above

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:49.340
5% and pay-out ratios under 60% suits TFSA compounding. Covered call ETF strategies such as

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:58.940
ZWC or QYLD add 4-8% annualized yield in sideways regimes. Position sizing matters and limit

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:06.060
covered call exposure to avoid capping upside during strong rallies. AI momentum investing uses

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:12.920
real-time sentiment and earnings revision data to ride sector leadership. Micron surge on AI

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:18.380
demand shows how individual investors can apply this by screening for companies with both

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:26.000
positive earnings revisions and volume spikes above the 20-day average. Size positions at 3-5%

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:33.260
of a TFSA to limit drawdowns. Canadian investors can implement it by pairing a US-listed AI name

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:41.160
with a CAD- hedged ETF wrapper to manage currency exposure. Intense rotational plays involve shifting

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:47.260
capital between sectors or themes based on short-term catalysts. Screen for stocks with fresh

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:55.120
12-month target increases from multiple brokers and check 5-day relative volume above 150% of the

00:03:55.120 --> 00:04:01.960
20-day average. Rotations have delivered the strongest alpha in the final 6-8 weeks of a quarter

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:09.380
when macro data shifts. Since we last covered these themes, the ongoing story of sector rotation has

00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:16.060
been the dominant driver. The ABB V-deal and Micron commentary both reinforced how catalysts in

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:23.720
healthcare and AI can create short-term opportunities even as broader tech sold off. Geopolitical

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:30.600
cross-currents added volatility with fresh US Iran tensions and Trump threats weighing on rate-cut odds.

